---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import NameTimeline from '../components/NameTimeline';
import { getLineage } from '../lib/data';

const data = getLineage();
const claims = data.flatMap((p) => p.claims);
const authorities = new Set(claims.map((c) => c.authority)).size;
const years = claims.map((c) => c.year);
const contested = data.filter((p) => p.n_candidates >= 3).length;
const disputed = data.filter((p) => p.confidence === 'disputed').length;
const alternatives = new Set(data.flatMap((p) => p.claims.filter((c) => c.role === 'alternative').map((c) => `${p.slug}|${c.taxon.split(' (')[0]}`))).size;
---
<Base title="Names through time" current="names" description="Five centuries of scholars trying to match Dioscorides' Greek plant names to modern species, and which match we model.">
  <div class="page flex flex-col gap-8 pb-16 pt-10">
    <div class="flex max-w-[820px] flex-col gap-2">
      <div class="eyebrow text-ochre">Then: the identification problem</div>
      <h1 class="h-display m-0 text-[clamp(34px,4vw,48px)]">Names through time</h1>
      <p class="m-0 text-[17px] text-muted">Before any climate model can run, someone has to decide which living plant Dioscorides meant by a Greek name. Since the Renaissance, physicians, botanists and philologists have disagreed. We read those identifications, cite them per plant and model the best-supported one. Where the debate is open, we say so on every page.</p>
    </div>
    <dl class="m-0 grid gap-x-8 gap-y-4 border-y border-rule py-5 [grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(min(100%,180px),1fr))]">
      <div><dt class="text-[13px] text-muted">Dated identification claims</dt><dd class="m-0 text-[28px] font-semibold">{claims.length}</dd></div>
      <div><dt class="text-[13px] text-muted">Authorities, {Math.min(...years)}–{Math.max(...years)}</dt><dd class="m-0 text-[28px] font-semibold">{authorities}</dd></div>
      <div><dt class="text-[13px] text-muted">Alternative candidate species</dt><dd class="m-0 text-[28px] font-semibold">{alternatives}</dd></div>
      <div><dt class="text-[13px] text-muted">Names with 3+ candidates · rated disputed</dt><dd class="m-0 text-[28px] font-semibold">{contested} <span class="text-[15px] font-normal text-muted">· {disputed}</span></dd></div>
    </dl>
    <NameTimeline client:load data={data} />
    <section aria-labelledby="h-why" class="flex max-w-[860px] flex-col gap-2.5 border-t-2 border-ochre pt-5">
      <h2 id="h-why" class="m-0 font-serif text-[28px] font-medium">Why this matters for the maps</h2>
      <ul class="m-0 flex flex-col gap-1.5 pl-5 text-[15px]">
        <li>A disputed name can change the answer: we may be modelling the wrong plant. Disputed plants carry a badge everywhere, and the Methods page reports the ranking with them removed.</li>
        <li>Some debates are about a group, not one species. Sideritis (mountain tea) is a genus of several Greek species that the EU monograph treats together.</li>
        <li>Pharmacopoeias inherited these identifications. Tracing them is how a 1st-century text links to a 21st-century EMA monograph.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>
